From 52041fd315310e6da8eae42bad8e369830e10cbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:20:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] kboot: hand the J713 external DCPs over to the kernel

iBoot starts both external display coprocessors and leaves them
quiesced, with their DARTs set up. Their CPU power domains stay
targeted on, gated by hardware while the controllers idle.

With the boot.bin line chosen.asahi,j713-dcpext=1 and after the
internal DCP was handed over, reserve each external DCP's firmware
memory, publish its firmware UUID and mark it ready for the kernel.
Only the power state words are read: the CPU domain and the
controller registers are left to the kernel, which wakes the running
controller over RTKit.

Reserve the external DCPs' OS log segments by physical address, as
the internal one's.

Document the option in docs/boot-options.md and aura.conf.example.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>

(backported from commit 21bf5eed43c4d49000ee80d05dd5e828560834df)
[j604: omacom m1n1 keeps its own boot-options.md and m1n1.conf.example (no aura-* option sections): only the J713 external display section and its config line are added, worded for the m1n1 configuration; kboot.c, pmgr.c/h and both tests as in aura #74 (merge 323ecafd)]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
